stem:
Consider the following graph-level IR transformation where a symbolic-shape function is specialized to concrete shapes at compile time:

BEFORE (symbolic):
```
func f(x : Tensor[N, K, f16], w : Tensor[K, M, f16]) -> Tensor[N, M, f16]:
    return matmul(x, w)
```
AFTER (specialized to N=32, K=4096, M=4096):
```
func f_32x4096x4096(x : Tensor[32, 4096, f16], w : Tensor[4096, 4096, f16]) -> Tensor[32, 4096, f16]:
    return matmul(x, w)
```
Which statement about this specialization is correct?

irSnippet:
// BEFORE (symbolic shape)
func.func @f(%x : tensor<?x?xf16>, %w : tensor<?x?xf16>) -> tensor<?x?xf16> {
  %0 = "custom.matmul"(%x, %w) : (tensor<?x?xf16>, tensor<?x?xf16>) -> tensor<?x?xf16>
  return %0 : tensor<?x?xf16>
}

// AFTER (shape-specialized)
func.func @f_32x4096x4096(%x : tensor<32x4096xf16>, %w : tensor<4096x4096xf16>) -> tensor<32x4096xf16> {
  %0 = "custom.matmul"(%x, %w) : (tensor<32x4096xf16>, tensor<4096x4096xf16>) -> tensor<32x4096xf16>
  return %0 : tensor<32x4096xf16>
}
